<p data-start=3D"1268" data-end=3D"1468">A healthy Ubuntu system usually ha=
s thousands of <code data-start=3D"1317" data-end=3D"1324">.list</code> fil=
es. If that count is unexpectedly low, your dpkg database has been damaged =
and we'll need to repair that before trusting package management.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1470" data-end=3D"1484">At this point:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1485" data-end=3D"1714">
<li data-section-id=3D"13adeqc" data-start=3D"1485" data-end=3D"1529">
<p data-start=3D"1487" data-end=3D"1529">=E2=9C=85 Kernel packages configur=
ed successfully.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1o9e06s" data-start=3D"1530" data-end=3D"1556">
<p data-start=3D"1532" data-end=3D"1556">=E2=9C=85 EC2 GRUB hook removed.</=
p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1r4dkje" data-start=3D"1557" data-end=3D"1585">
<p data-start=3D"1559" data-end=3D"1585">=E2=9D=8C <code data-start=3D"1561=
" data-end=3D"1570">grub-pc</code> still failing.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"ap0hyu" data-start=3D"1586" data-end=3D"1623">
<p data-start=3D"1588" data-end=3D"1623">=E2=9D=8C <code data-start=3D"1590=
" data-end=3D"1608">clamav-freshclam</code> still failing.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1perbu3" data-start=3D"1624" data-end=3D"1714">
<p data-start=3D"1626" data-end=3D"1714">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Possible dpkg d=
atabase corruption due to the massive number of missing <code data-start=3D=
"1700" data-end=3D"1707">.list</code> files.</p>
</li>
</ul>
