<p data-start=3D"198" data-end=3D"229">This is <strong data-start=3D"206" d=
ata-end=3D"228">not a GRUB problem</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"231" data-end=3D"341"><code data-start=3D"231" data-end=3D=
"249">grub-pc.postinst</code> is asking debconf to load templates from the =
package <strong data-start=3D"303" data-end=3D"310">ucf</strong>, and debco=
nf cannot find them.</p>
<p data-start=3D"343" data-end=3D"375">That usually means one of these:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"377" data-end=3D"566">
<li data-section-id=3D"irlr0r" data-start=3D"377" data-end=3D"403">
<p data-start=3D"380" data-end=3D"403"><code data-start=3D"380" data-end=3D=
"385">ucf</code> is not installed.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1nhrbzv" data-start=3D"404" data-end=3D"436">
<p data-start=3D"407" data-end=3D"436"><code data-start=3D"407" data-end=3D=
"412">ucf</code> is partially installed.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"14bmj6e" data-start=3D"437" data-end=3D"491">
<p data-start=3D"440" data-end=3D"491">Files under <code data-start=3D"452"=
 data-end=3D"478">/var/lib/dpkg/info/ucf.*</code> are missing.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"oymvjs" data-start=3D"492" data-end=3D"566">
<p data-start=3D"495" data-end=3D"566">Your <code data-start=3D"500" data-e=
nd=3D"534">/var/cache/debconf/templates.dat</code> or debconf database is d=
amaged.</p>
</li>
</ol>
