><div class=3D"markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark=
 markdown-new-styling"><p data-start=3D"0" data-end=3D"95">Looking at your =
screenshots, I don't think the BMS settings themselves are the primary prob=
lem.</p>
<p data-start=3D"97" data-end=3D"120">A few things stand out:</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"lvh5gb" data-start=3D"122" data-end=3D"149">What you=
r settings show</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"150" data-end=3D"278">
<li data-section-id=3D"f2isb9" data-start=3D"150" data-end=3D"198">
<p data-start=3D"152" data-end=3D"198">Cell UVP (undervoltage protection): =
<strong data-start=3D"188" data-end=3D"198">3.100V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"c0895x" data-start=3D"199" data-end=3D"246">
<p data-start=3D"201" data-end=3D"246">Cell UVPR (undervoltage recovery): <=
strong data-start=3D"236" data-end=3D"246">3.300V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1n4j69g" data-start=3D"247" data-end=3D"278">
<p data-start=3D"249" data-end=3D"278">Power Off Voltage: <strong data-star=
t=3D"268" data-end=3D"278">2.790V</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"280" data-end=3D"411">Those are quite different from the 3=
.2V/3.36V values in your earlier screenshot. The JK BMS currently appears t=
o be configured for:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"412" data-end=3D"475">
<li data-section-id=3D"12rjrln" data-start=3D"412" data-end=3D"442">
<p data-start=3D"414" data-end=3D"442">Cutoff at <strong data-start=3D"424"=
 data-end=3D"442">3.10V per cell</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1h0jek7" data-start=3D"443" data-end=3D"475">
<p data-start=3D"445" data-end=3D"475">Recovery at <strong data-start=3D"45=
7" data-end=3D"475">3.30V per cell</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"477" data-end=3D"513">That's actually fairly conservative.=
</p>
<hr data-start=3D"515" data-end=3D"518">
<h3 data-section-id=3D"7627a8" data-start=3D"520" data-end=3D"555">What hap=
pened during the fault?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"557" data-end=3D"582">In the center screenshot:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"583" data-end=3D"720">
<li data-section-id=3D"12h2pi7" data-start=3D"583" data-end=3D"609">
<p data-start=3D"585" data-end=3D"609">Pack voltage: <strong data-start=3D"=
599" data-end=3D"609">39.37V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"q1fe84" data-start=3D"610" data-end=3D"644">
<p data-start=3D"612" data-end=3D"644">Average cell voltage: <strong data-s=
tart=3D"634" data-end=3D"644">2.812V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"ai1f0f" data-start=3D"645" data-end=3D"670">
<p data-start=3D"647" data-end=3D"670">Lowest cell: <strong data-start=3D"6=
60" data-end=3D"670">2.799V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"v4gti0" data-start=3D"671" data-end=3D"720">
<p data-start=3D"673" data-end=3D"720">BMS status: <strong data-start=3D"68=
5" data-end=3D"720">Protection - Cell under voltage</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"722" data-end=3D"794">This means the cells really did fall=
 well below the 3.10V UVP threshold.</p>
<p data-start=3D"796" data-end=3D"818">The question is <em data-start=3D"81=
2" data-end=3D"817">why</em>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"820" data-end=3D"823">
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1lpma14" data-start=3D"825" data-end=3D"864">The clu=
e is in the right screenshot</h3>
<p data-start=3D"866" data-end=3D"893">The right screenshot shows:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"895" data-end=3D"1062">
<li data-section-id=3D"1vfn064" data-start=3D"895" data-end=3D"921">
<p data-start=3D"897" data-end=3D"921">Pack voltage: <strong data-start=3D"=
911" data-end=3D"921">44.94V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"jf0ey5" data-start=3D"922" data-end=3D"956">
<p data-start=3D"924" data-end=3D"956">Average cell voltage: <strong data-s=
tart=3D"946" data-end=3D"956">3.210V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"nsuu9i" data-start=3D"957" data-end=3D"982">
<p data-start=3D"959" data-end=3D"982">Lowest cell: <strong data-start=3D"9=
72" data-end=3D"982">3.168V</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1ts0a0r" data-start=3D"983" data-end=3D"1006">
<p data-start=3D"985" data-end=3D"1006">Cell spread: <strong data-start=3D"=
998" data-end=3D"1006">72mV</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"rhxl1r" data-start=3D"1007" data-end=3D"1062">
<p data-start=3D"1009" data-end=3D"1062">Yet still showing <strong data-sta=
rt=3D"1027" data-end=3D"1062">Protection - Cell under voltage</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1064" data-end=3D"1114">This is classic JK BMS behavior af=
ter a UVP event.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1116" data-end=3D"1184">The BMS tripped because one cell d=
ropped below 3.10V <strong data-start=3D"1169" data-end=3D"1183">under load=
</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1186" data-end=3D"1251">After the load disappeared, the ce=
ll voltage rebounded to 3.168V.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1253" data-end=3D"1261">However:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1262" data-end=3D"1367">
<li data-section-id=3D"1l3ky7q" data-start=3D"1262" data-end=3D"1294">
<p data-start=3D"1264" data-end=3D"1294">Discharge MOSFET remained OFF.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"6zxxcs" data-start=3D"1295" data-end=3D"1326">
<p data-start=3D"1297" data-end=3D"1326">Recovery wasn't complete yet.</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1k5xg85" data-start=3D"1327" data-end=3D"1367">
<p data-start=3D"1329" data-end=3D"1367">Or the protection flag hadn't clea=
red.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"1369" data-end=3D"1372">
<h3 data-section-id=3D"18isucq" data-start=3D"1374" data-end=3D"1403">Why d=
id it go below 3.1V?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1405" data-end=3D"1463">The most likely explanation is <st=
rong data-start=3D"1436" data-end=3D"1462">voltage sag under load</strong>.=
</p>
<p data-start=3D"1465" data-end=3D"1477">For example:</p>
<p data-start=3D"1479" data-end=3D"1487">At rest:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1488" data-end=3D"1502">
<li data-section-id=3D"36o7f5" data-start=3D"1488" data-end=3D"1502">
<p data-start=3D"1490" data-end=3D"1502">Cell =3D 3.18V</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1504" data-end=3D"1523">Under a heavy load:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1524" data-end=3D"1564">
<li data-section-id=3D"pcms35" data-start=3D"1524" data-end=3D"1564">
<p data-start=3D"1526" data-end=3D"1564">Cell instantly drops to 3.05V or l=
ower</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1566" data-end=3D"1575">BMS sees:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1576" data-end=3D"1603">
<li data-section-id=3D"sq00j4" data-start=3D"1576" data-end=3D"1591">
<p data-start=3D"1578" data-end=3D"1591">3.05V &lt; 3.10V</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"lfkafr" data-start=3D"1592" data-end=3D"1603">
<p data-start=3D"1594" data-end=3D"1603">Trips UVP</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1605" data-end=3D"1621">Load disappears:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1622" data-end=3D"1646">
<li data-section-id=3D"rd889a" data-start=3D"1622" data-end=3D"1646">
<p data-start=3D"1624" data-end=3D"1646">Cell rebounds to 3.17V</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1648" data-end=3D"1737">You never actually see the low vol=
tage because it only existed while current was flowing.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1739" data-end=3D"1742">
<h3 data-section-id=3D"120fn70" data-start=3D"1744" data-end=3D"1776">Anoth=
er clue: Cell imbalance</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1778" data-end=3D"1805">The right screenshot shows:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1807" data-end=3D"1853">
<li data-section-id=3D"9l53rq" data-start=3D"1807" data-end=3D"1830">
<p data-start=3D"1809" data-end=3D"1830">Highest cell =E2=89=88 3.241V</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1yb9mw4" data-start=3D"1831" data-end=3D"1853">
<p data-start=3D"1833" data-end=3D"1853">Lowest cell =E2=89=88 3.168V</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1855" data-end=3D"1866">Difference:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1867" data-end=3D"1877">
<li data-section-id=3D"14rjiom" data-start=3D"1867" data-end=3D"1877">
<p data-start=3D"1869" data-end=3D"1877"><strong data-start=3D"1869" data-e=
nd=3D"1877">72mV</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1879" data-end=3D"1958">For a 14-cell pack that's not terr=
ible, but it isn't perfectly balanced either.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1960" data-end=3D"1988">The middle screenshot shows:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1990" data-end=3D"2043">
<li data-section-id=3D"17e3fcr" data-start=3D"1990" data-end=3D"2007">
<p data-start=3D"1992" data-end=3D"2007">Cell 5 =3D 2.799V</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"l34982" data-start=3D"2008" data-end=3D"2025">
<p data-start=3D"2010" data-end=3D"2025">Cell 3 =3D 2.800V</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"17ntmex" data-start=3D"2026" data-end=3D"2043">
<p data-start=3D"2028" data-end=3D"2043">Cell 7 =3D 2.799V</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2045" data-end=3D"2105">Those cells appear to be the first=
 ones reaching the bottom.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2107" data-end=3D"2110">
<h3 data-section-id=3D"10mezuj" data-start=3D"2112" data-end=3D"2149">I'd c=
heck the Solis settings next</h3>
<p data-start=3D"2151" data-end=3D"2233">The inverter should normally stop =
discharging <strong data-start=3D"2197" data-end=3D"2207">before</strong> t=
he BMS has to intervene.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2235" data-end=3D"2251">Can you tell me:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"2253" data-end=3D"2487">
<li data-section-id=3D"15iv6yf" data-start=3D"2253" data-end=3D"2342">
<p data-start=3D"2256" data-end=3D"2342">Is this a <strong data-start=3D"22=
66" data-end=3D"2280">14S Li-ion</strong> pack? (The voltages suggest 14S N=
MC/NCA rather than LiFePO=E2=82=84.)</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"frdfo0" data-start=3D"2343" data-end=3D"2381">
<p data-start=3D"2346" data-end=3D"2381">What exact Solis model do you have=
?</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1jpdjnn" data-start=3D"2382" data-end=3D"2487">
<p data-start=3D"2385" data-end=3D"2487">Is the battery communicating with =
the inverter via CAN/RS485, or is the Solis running in voltage mode?</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"2489" data-end=3D"2644">If the Solis is running purely on =
voltage settings, I suspect its low-battery cutoff is set too low and it's =
driving the pack into the BMS protection zone.</p>
