<p data-start=3D"189" data-end=3D"252">and Home Assistant is also monitorin=
g the aggregate controller.</p>
<p data-start=3D"254" data-end=3D"329">In that architecture, there are <str=
ong data-start=3D"286" data-end=3D"328">three separate layers making decisi=
ons</strong>:</p>
<ol data-start=3D"331" data-end=3D"430">
<li data-section-id=3D"nlqoct" data-start=3D"331" data-end=3D"367">
<p data-start=3D"334" data-end=3D"367">Individual JK BMS on each battery</p=
>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1iiwbdp" data-start=3D"368" data-end=3D"408">
<p data-start=3D"371" data-end=3D"408">The aggregate/"middle man" controlle=
r</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"18aymzy" data-start=3D"409" data-end=3D"430">
<p data-start=3D"412" data-end=3D"430">The Solis inverter</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start=3D"432" data-end=3D"435">
<h2 data-section-id=3D"14vutw6" data-start=3D"437" data-end=3D"502">Why wou=
ld a cell reach 2.79V before the BMS stopped discharge?</h2>
<p data-start=3D"504" data-end=3D"548">In theory, it shouldn't stay there f=
or long.</p>
<p data-start=3D"550" data-end=3D"574">What usually happens is:</p>
<h3 data-section-id=3D"1p2c47y" data-start=3D"576" data-end=3D"622">Scenari=
o 1: Voltage sag during a high load</h3>
<p data-start=3D"624" data-end=3D"638">A cell may be:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"640" data-end=3D"768">
<li data-section-id=3D"5gpw0y" data-start=3D"640" data-end=3D"655">
<p data-start=3D"642" data-end=3D"655">3.15V at rest</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1h3tmo" data-start=3D"656" data-end=3D"675">
<p data-start=3D"658" data-end=3D"675">Large load starts</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1pq55a1" data-start=3D"676" data-end=3D"706">
<p data-start=3D"678" data-end=3D"706">Cell instantly sags to 2.79V</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1kjrt6" data-start=3D"707" data-end=3D"725">
<p data-start=3D"709" data-end=3D"725">JK BMS trips UVP</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"ctjqy5" data-start=3D"726" data-end=3D"750">
<p data-start=3D"728" data-end=3D"750">Discharge MOSFET opens</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"11104d0" data-start=3D"751" data-end=3D"768">
<p data-start=3D"753" data-end=3D"768">Load disappears</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"770" data-end=3D"817">When you later inspect the logs, it =
looks like:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"819" data-end=3D"863">
<p data-start=3D"821" data-end=3D"863">"How did it get to 2.79V if UVP is 3=
.10V?"</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"865" data-end=3D"872">Answer:</p>
<blockquote data-start=3D"874" data-end=3D"936">
<p data-start=3D"876" data-end=3D"936">It crossed 3.10V momentarily under l=
oad and the BMS reacted.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start=3D"938" data-end=3D"1039">The BMS isn't preventing the voltag=
e from <em data-start=3D"980" data-end=3D"986">ever</em> going below 3.10V.=
 It's reacting once it detects it.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1041" data-end=3D"1044">
<h3 data-section-id=3D"18dtu01" data-start=3D"1046" data-end=3D"1113">Scena=
rio 2: The aggregate controller was still requesting power</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1115" data-end=3D"1179">This is actually the more interest=
ing possibility in your setup.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1181" data-end=3D"1189">Suppose:</p>
<p data-start=3D"1191" data-end=3D"1201">Battery A:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1202" data-end=3D"1223">
<li data-section-id=3D"lblgwd" data-start=3D"1202" data-end=3D"1211">
<p data-start=3D"1204" data-end=3D"1211">Healthy</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"d94tw8" data-start=3D"1212" data-end=3D"1223">
<p data-start=3D"1214" data-end=3D"1223">3.2V/cell</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1225" data-end=3D"1235">Battery B:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1236" data-end=3D"1259">
<li data-section-id=3D"1cs8le2" data-start=3D"1236" data-end=3D"1259">
<p data-start=3D"1238" data-end=3D"1259">Weakest cell at 3.11V</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1261" data-end=3D"1291">The aggregate controller sees:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1293" data-end=3D"1374">
<li data-section-id=3D"105pi5u" data-start=3D"1293" data-end=3D"1342">
<p data-start=3D"1295" data-end=3D"1342">Combined battery voltage still loo=
ks acceptable</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1hqo1fz" data-start=3D"1343" data-end=3D"1374">
<p data-start=3D"1345" data-end=3D"1374">Solis continues drawing power</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1376" data-end=3D"1381">Then:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1383" data-end=3D"1461">
<li data-section-id=3D"2njh3l" data-start=3D"1383" data-end=3D"1422">
<p data-start=3D"1385" data-end=3D"1422">Weak cell in Battery B drops to 3.=
05V</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"12w3suu" data-start=3D"1423" data-end=3D"1437">
<p data-start=3D"1425" data-end=3D"1437">JK trips UVP</p>
</li>
<li data-section-id=3D"1y9oa38" data-start=3D"1438" data-end=3D"1461">
<p data-start=3D"1440" data-end=3D"1461">Battery B disconnects</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1463" data-end=3D"1517">Now Battery A suddenly has to supp=
ort the entire load.</p>
<p data-start=3D"1519" data-end=3D"1561">Depending on timing, things can ge=
t messy.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1563" data-end=3D"1566">
<h2 data-section-id=3D"uf28hj" data-start=3D"1568" data-end=3D"1605">The nu=
mber I'd really like to know</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1607" data-end=3D"1635">On the battery that hit UVP:</p>
<p data-start=3D"1637" data-end=3D"1658">What was the current?</p>
<p data-start=3D"1660" data-end=3D"1685">The JK logs usually show:</p>
<ul data-start=3D"1687" data-end=3D"1732">
<li data-section-id=3D"1dkyz70" data-start=3D"1687" data-end=3D"1704">
<p data-start=3D"1689" data-end=3D"1704">Battery current</p>
